{
  "id": "hoses___water_volume_discharge_flow_vs__pressure",
  "title": "Hoses - Water Volume Discharge Flow vs. Pressure",
  "description": "Water discharge through hoses - pressure ranging 10 - 200 psi (0.75 - 14 bar). Calculate water flow discharge rates based on hose diameter and pressure.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Water Discharge Through Hoses\n\nWater discharge through hoses at various pressures and hose diameters.\n\n**Imperial Units:** Water discharge through 100 feet hoses at pressures ranging 10 - 200 psi\n\n**Metric Units:** Water discharge through 30 m hoses at pressures ranging 0.75 - 14 bar\n\n### Conversion Factors\n- 1 psi = 6.9 kPa = 0.069 bar\n- 1 ft (foot) = 0.3048 m\n- 1 gal (US)/min = 6.30888×10⁻⁵ m³/s = 0.227 m³/h"
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Hose Nominal Diameter (inches)",
        "Internal Diameter (inches)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "1/8",
          0.125
        ],
        [
          "3/16",
          0.1875
        ],
        [
          "1/4",
          0.25
        ],
        [
          "5/16",
          0.3125
        ],
        [
          "3/8",
          0.375
        ],
        [
          "7/16",
          0.4375
        ],
        [
          "1/2",
          0.5
        ],
        [
          "5/8",
          0.625
        ],
        [
          "3/4",
          0.75
        ],
        [
          "7/8",
          0.875
        ],
        [
          "1",
          1
        ],
        [
          "1 1/4",
          1.25
        ],
        [
          "1 1/2",
          1.5
        ],
        [
          "2",
